00:31:15.360 --> 00:31:18.940
did come to live, to die, to rise again, to ascend,

00:31:19.060 --> 00:31:22.120
to reign forever and ever, and now we're with that guy.

00:31:23.460 --> 00:31:25.100
This is what we live in now.

00:31:25.200 --> 00:31:27.540
This is the truth that sets us free.

00:31:28.380 --> 00:31:29.600
And so when we think about this,

00:31:30.200 --> 00:31:32.140
the rebellious spiritual powers of this world,

00:31:32.220 --> 00:31:34.780
they are real, but we do not need to fear them.

00:31:35.340 --> 00:31:36.980
By the blood of Jesus Christ

00:31:36.980 --> 00:31:39.160
and this testimony that we have in him,

00:31:39.280 --> 00:31:46.560
we have overcome. So all of this becomes this new reality that we now live in. And lastly,

00:31:47.100 --> 00:31:52.960
as we get to verse 7, we find this, that God shows his kindness to us in Christ.

00:31:54.340 --> 00:32:00.560
God shows his kindness to us in Christ. You know what Paul is saying? What is God trying to show us

00:32:00.560 --> 00:32:07.800
here? What is God trying to show to the world by everything that he's done for us? He's trying

00:32:07.800 --> 00:32:15.780
to show us how kind he is. He's trying to show us how patient he is, how loving, how generous,

00:32:16.480 --> 00:32:22.700
how gracious, how merciful. If I read that verse again, it says, so that in the coming ages he might

00:32:22.700 --> 00:32:29.940
show the immeasurable riches of his grace and kindness toward us in Christ Jesus. And here's

00:32:29.940 --> 00:32:38.080
where I want to just kind of make this connection. For a lot of us, we have understanding of these

00:32:38.080 --> 00:32:42.800
things these verses teach. Maybe today you're realizing, okay, it's more than I thought it was.

00:32:42.800 --> 00:32:49.560
Okay, great, great. But how does that affect us on a daily basis? How does it change our hearts?

00:32:50.580 --> 00:32:53.640
How does it change our relationships? How does it change the way that we live?

00:32:54.560 --> 00:32:59.200
Well, let me just put it to you as a question first. What motivates you to follow Jesus?

00:32:59.940 --> 00:33:06.400
What motivates you to do the simple things we do in a life of faith and following him?

00:33:07.480 --> 00:33:12.020
Why do we come to a Sunday celebration here or with another church?

00:33:13.240 --> 00:33:15.700
Why do we open the Bible and read its pages?

00:33:16.980 --> 00:33:17.760
Why do we pray?

00:33:18.400 --> 00:33:18.980
Why do we serve?

00:33:19.060 --> 00:33:20.560
Why do we do all of these things?

00:33:21.480 --> 00:33:22.960
And I ask us that question.

00:33:22.960 --> 00:33:26.420
because I think what God really wants for us

00:33:26.420 --> 00:33:29.020
is to do all these things in response

00:33:29.020 --> 00:33:32.240
to his kindness, mercy, and grace

00:33:32.240 --> 00:33:36.080
that we would love because he first loved us.

00:33:36.740 --> 00:33:38.520
But I realize that many of us,

00:33:38.860 --> 00:33:40.460
in fact, probably most of us,

00:33:40.640 --> 00:33:43.500
are still kind of running on a different operating system.

00:33:44.880 --> 00:33:47.560
And I don't know if you've ever made an operating system switch,

00:33:47.620 --> 00:33:49.280
like you've gone from Mac to PC

00:33:49.280 --> 00:33:52.060
or you've gone from Android to Apple

00:33:52.060 --> 00:33:52.860
or something like that.

00:33:52.960 --> 00:33:54.440
It's awkward for a little while, right?

00:33:54.860 --> 00:33:57.780
And it's frustrating because you don't know where to find stuff

00:33:57.780 --> 00:33:59.740
and something that seems like it should be a certain place,

00:33:59.800 --> 00:34:00.840
it's not there, it's somewhere else.

00:34:00.960 --> 00:34:02.780
And making that shift is hard.

00:34:03.520 --> 00:34:07.380
For some of us, we're actually running on this old operating system

00:34:07.380 --> 00:34:11.860
that's built on things like fear and performance

00:34:11.860 --> 00:34:17.560
and comparison and achievement and consumerism

00:34:17.560 --> 00:34:22.920
and jealousy and insecurity, all that kind of stuff.

00:34:22.960 --> 00:34:28.680
we're still running on that, even while we know the truth of what Christ has done for us.

00:34:29.780 --> 00:34:34.220
And, you know, so we think about things like, well, why should I read the Bible?

00:34:36.040 --> 00:34:40.140
Pastor told me I'm not going to earn anything from God from reading the Bible, so why would I bother?

00:34:41.100 --> 00:34:43.360
Because we're still thinking of things in terms of earning.

00:34:44.780 --> 00:34:48.900
Maybe we think like, well, if I don't serve, does that make me a bad Christian?

00:34:49.460 --> 00:34:52.040
I guess I better serve so that I can be a good Christian.

00:34:52.960 --> 00:34:58.720
and we worry about that, and it's still about our own performance. It's about being good enough.

00:35:00.320 --> 00:35:04.860
Maybe we think, oh, should I become a member of the church? What am I going to get out of that?

00:35:05.980 --> 00:35:13.780
We still think very consumeristically about these things. Maybe we think, man, if I become a leader

00:35:13.780 --> 00:35:20.140
in the church, well, maybe then that person whose approval I want so much will finally accept me and

00:35:20.140 --> 00:35:27.840
approve of me and tell me that I'm good enough. That insecurity drives things that we ultimately

00:35:27.840 --> 00:35:34.120
would want to do for God. There is so many of us struggle deeply with these things. It infiltrates

00:35:34.120 --> 00:35:39.420
everything in our lives. And I just want you to know today, God does not want any of that for you.

00:35:40.080 --> 00:35:47.820
We need an entirely new operating system built on love and mercy and grace. God's kindness toward

00:35:47.820 --> 00:35:54.000
us in Christ Jesus. And that looks like things like, God, you've been so compassionate to me.

00:35:54.720 --> 00:35:57.600
God, I just want to be compassionate toward that other hurting person now.

00:35:58.800 --> 00:36:07.000
God, Jesus, you serve me so selflessly. I want to serve others now. God, you've been so good to

00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:11.780
me. I just want to worship you. I want to come and worship you, and not because I have to,

00:36:11.780 --> 00:36:18.720
but because I want to. And God, your love is so great. God, I want to hear you speak to me

00:36:18.720 --> 00:36:25.980
through your word. You love me so much. And all those things that previously were done out of

00:36:25.980 --> 00:36:33.300
guilt, out of comparison, out of shame, out of insecurity, suddenly get transformed as God

00:36:33.300 --> 00:36:39.280
changes our hearts to say, God, now I can do these things with gratitude, with love, with

00:36:39.280 --> 00:36:45.180
thankfulness, with a heart that desires to love God and love people because of everything that

00:36:45.180 --> 00:36:51.860
God's done for me, because of the kindness that's been shown to me by the Lord. This is hard.

00:36:52.940 --> 00:36:58.700
And I think for some of us, this might actually be a long battle. But I want to invite you into

00:36:58.700 --> 00:37:03.740
that. And even ask the Lord to search your heart this morning, because within our church family

00:37:03.740 --> 00:37:09.500
here. I want us to know, I don't want anyone in our church to do things because they feel guilty,

00:37:09.620 --> 00:37:13.040
because they just feel obligated, because they feel like they have to, to prove themselves,

00:37:13.120 --> 00:37:18.820
any of that. We don't want that to be why we do what we do. We want everything we do to be a

00:37:18.820 --> 00:37:24.780
response to God's mercy and grace. And that's something I've had to wrestle with. Many of us

00:37:24.780 --> 00:37:29.000
have to wrestle with. We may have to wrestle with for a lifetime, but that's why we continually come

00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:35.180
back to Jesus and what it is that he has done for us. So living our higher calling really starts

00:37:35.180 --> 00:37:40.620
with seeing ourselves clearly, and then responding to God's mercy and grace. And that's why if I could

00:37:40.620 --> 00:37:45.320
kind of sum it up this way this morning, that our higher calling is to receive God's grace and

00:37:45.320 --> 00:37:51.860
rejoice in his love. To receive God's grace and rejoice in his love, and let that then be the

00:37:51.860 --> 00:37:58.060
foundation. Let that be the core. Let that be the center of our whole lives and everything that we do.

00:37:58.700 --> 00:38:02.760
And another thing that I realize is that the gap between where we are now

00:38:02.760 --> 00:38:06.380
and the full inheritance that we have in Jesus Christ

00:38:06.380 --> 00:38:09.780
is often bridged through prayer and steps of faith.

00:38:10.380 --> 00:38:13.120
Prayer and steps of faith, that's what really helps us

00:38:13.120 --> 00:38:17.860
to move from still being trapped in the old life

00:38:17.860 --> 00:38:20.100
and then being able to live in the new life,

00:38:20.200 --> 00:38:22.200
the new inheritance that we have in Christ.

00:38:22.560 --> 00:38:25.380
And so if I could give us one practical suggestion for this week,

00:38:25.380 --> 00:38:27.760
is to read today's passage daily

00:38:27.760 --> 00:38:30.500
and then pray for God to change your motivations.

00:38:31.220 --> 00:38:32.400
I think this is really helpful

00:38:32.400 --> 00:38:34.540
because again, half of you were gone last Sunday.

00:38:34.900 --> 00:38:36.180
But last Sunday when we went through,

00:38:36.280 --> 00:38:37.480
there was a prayer that Paul prayed

00:38:37.480 --> 00:38:38.680
at the end of Ephesians 1.

00:38:39.160 --> 00:38:41.640
And a challenge I gave to everyone here last week was,

00:38:41.920 --> 00:38:43.500
hey, can we pray that passage

00:38:43.500 --> 00:38:46.080
for someone in your life every day this week?

00:38:46.420 --> 00:38:47.580
And so I've actually been doing that

00:38:47.580 --> 00:38:48.800
with my family this whole week.

00:38:48.860 --> 00:38:50.420
Every day, just praying,

00:38:50.740 --> 00:38:53.500
God, enlighten the eyes of our hearts

00:38:53.500 --> 00:38:56.120
so that we can see with our hearts

00:38:56.120 --> 00:38:58.020
the hope we have in you

00:38:58.020 --> 00:38:59.820
and the power that you have

00:38:59.820 --> 00:39:01.040
that raised Jesus from the dead.

00:39:01.200 --> 00:39:02.560
I've been praying that for my family

00:39:02.560 --> 00:39:03.260
every day this week.

00:39:03.320 --> 00:39:04.180
It's been really good for me.

00:39:04.260 --> 00:39:05.220
I hope it's good for them

00:39:05.220 --> 00:39:07.060
and I hope God's answering that prayer

00:39:07.060 --> 00:39:09.180
but I realize daily reflecting,

00:39:09.380 --> 00:39:11.180
praying through these things is so good

00:39:11.180 --> 00:39:13.520
and especially if you're realizing,

00:39:14.180 --> 00:39:15.240
wow, yeah, I've been trapped

00:39:15.240 --> 00:39:16.700
in the old operating system.

00:39:17.200 --> 00:39:19.100
I've been trapped in the old way of seeing things.

00:39:19.460 --> 00:39:21.840
I've been living my Christian life

00:39:21.840 --> 00:39:27.220
driven not by the things of God, but by the things of this world. This would be especially important.

00:39:27.760 --> 00:39:32.160
See, I'm going to pull out this passage daily, seven verses, and I'm going to pray and ask God

00:39:32.160 --> 00:39:37.680
to change my heart. What would it do for you if you woke up in the morning and got ready to go

00:39:37.680 --> 00:39:43.280
to class or to work or to raise your family or all the other things that you do? And maybe you

00:39:43.280 --> 00:39:46.820
wake up in the morning just feeling burdened, weighed down. Okay, I guess I've just got to do

00:39:46.820 --> 00:39:52.760
these things. I don't want to disappoint anyone. I got to prove myself. I got to be good enough in

00:39:52.760 --> 00:39:58.620
all these ways. What if you open up the Bible, read these seven verses, and said, God, change my

00:39:58.620 --> 00:40:05.240
heart. Change my motivations. Do something in me, God, because God, I want today when I serve my

00:40:05.240 --> 00:40:10.200
spouse, I want to do that, God, not just to keep that other person from being angry at me. I want

00:40:10.200 --> 00:40:14.500
to do that because you've served me, God. I want to do that out of love. God, I want to do well in

00:40:14.500 --> 00:40:19.200
school, not because my security is built on my grades and my academic performance. I want to do

00:40:19.200 --> 00:40:24.180
well in school because, God, it's good to be alive today. Because, God, you made me alive in Jesus

00:40:24.180 --> 00:40:29.660
Christ. You gave me life not just for now but for eternity. God, it's so good to be alive today. I

00:40:29.660 --> 00:40:34.200
want to use every moment that I can to worship you, to use the gifts and opportunities you've

00:40:34.200 --> 00:40:40.540
given me. God, change my heart. God, I want to get up and go to life group today. And not because I

00:40:40.540 --> 00:40:44.180
have to, not because somebody's going to be disappointed in me if I don't, not because I'm

00:40:44.180 --> 00:40:49.580
the one who has to bring the chips. But God, I want to go there because I want to know you more.

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:54.080
I want to lift up my brothers and sisters. I want to encourage my community. I want to grow in

00:40:54.080 --> 00:40:59.200
